From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Mon, 4 Aug 2025 10:02:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] make compatible with darwin newfs_msdos

Summary:
# Motivation:
This binary is part of the list of cuttlefish host binaries. The macro is already defined in macos sdk

# Overview:
- only define macro if not already defined to avoid compilation error

Test Plan:
```
. build/envsetup.sh
 lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug
 m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz -k &> ~/build.logs.txt
```

Rollback Plan:

Reviewers: tcare, #cuttlefish-cross-platform, benthomas

Reviewed By: tcare

Subscribers: ryanyu, #wearables_emulators

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.intern.facebook.com/D79568660

Tags: aarch64
---
 freebsd-compat.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/freebsd-compat.h b/freebsd-compat.h
index 7ab9d70..5f0ff2b 100644
--- a/freebsd-compat.h
+++ b/freebsd-compat.h
@@ -12,7 +12,9 @@
 #define nitems(x) (sizeof((x))/sizeof((x)[0]))
 
 // This is used as the size of the write buffer of sectors.
+#ifndef MAXPHYS
 #define MAXPHYS (1024 * 1024)
+#endif
 
 // On glibc, these headers use `__unused` as an identifier, so drag them in
 // first.
